From e4ba5aa65f891d92a5d89c4bb4c7bb7f455e9be2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dixonSolutions <203963471+dixonSolutions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:10:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 30/64] arm64: dts: exynos: exynos9810: Add sysreg, USI and
 HSI2C nodes

Describe the CMGP, PERIC0 and PERIC1 system registers, which hold the
USI SW_CONF registers, and the HSI2C channels that have devices on the
Galaxy Tab Active3, plus the four camera I2C channels:

  channel           HSI2C       SW_CONF          IRQ  pins (func)
  I2C_CAM0..3       1086..1089  none             424..427 gpc0-0..7 (2)
  PERIC0 USI01_I2C  10480000    PERIC0 + 0x1010  401  gpp0-6/7 (3)
  PERIC1 USI07_USI  108c0000    PERIC1 + 0x1024  430  gpp4-4/5 (2)
  PERIC1 USI08_USI  108e0000    PERIC1 + 0x102c  432  gpp5-0/1 (2)
  PERIC1 USI09_I2C  10910000    PERIC1 + 0x1038  435  gpp5-6/7 (3)
  USI_CMGP00        14300000    CMGP + 0x2000      0  gpm0-0/gpm1-0 (2)
  USI_CMGP03        14360000    CMGP + 0x2030      6  gpm14-0/gpm15-0 (2)

Addresses, interrupts and pin functions are from the vendor device tree
(hsi2c_N and usi_N nodes), the sysreg bases from the vendor PMU CAL
sequences. Clocks are left to the boards until there is an Exynos9810
clock driver. All nodes are disabled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
